People said Singapore is "boring"?

Their definition of a good life is a life full of "fun", not 'boring' stuff that you 'see' in Singapore?

Then perhaps their idea of a 'not boring/fun' life is :

- taking drugs until you die from overdose;
- or selling drugs that cause irreparable harm to & destroying countless people, families, communities, societies & countries;
- or owning a gun that you use to shoot anyone you want;
- or live in a place that fatal shootings happen almost everyday including in schools that take the lives of innocent children, youth, educators & school staff & injuring & traumatising countless others for life;
- or partying in clubs by drinking until you throw up & become a nuisance of yourself such as getting into fights or molesting women;
- or worse, driving when drunk then KILLING innocent people on the roads;
- or live in a place where you can't walk the streets alone especially at night & especially for women or children for fear of being robbed, molested, raped or even killed;
- or seeing homeless people on practically every street corner as a normal thing such that you are blind to it & have no sympathy or empathy for such people.

Perhaps the 'best' life for people who said Singapore is 'boring' is when they can do/say whatever they want & then GET AWAY WITH IT.
No punishment.
No consequences.
Nothing.

None of that can be found in Singapore. Which explains why many said Singapore is 'boring'.

Well then, such people are welcome to leave Singapore & find some place where they CAN have such a 'not boring/fun' life.
